Sprites sampling exactly on texel edges round down, like parallelograms

A nearest-sampled sprite whose UV tracks the position 1:1 with an off-grid
top-left corner (Y = -0.5, V = 0.5) samples exactly on texel edges. The GS DDA
rounds down there (as the existing parallelogram heuristic assumes); paraLLEl-GS
picked the next texel. Dynasty Warriors 5 resets Z through such a sprite
(alpha-tested on the frame itself), so the reset missed the last row of the
far terrain and the near terrain failed its depth test there: one-row seams
across the battlefield. Verified offline on a recorded frame: the result now
matches the CPU reference renderer on those rows.

slangmosh.hpp carries the recompiled triangle_setup SPIR-V
(tools/parallel_gs_splice_shader.py, glslc -fshader-stage=comp --target-env=vulkan1.1 -O).

